{title: Hosanna in the Highest}
{subtitle: Matthew 21:1–11; Luke 19:37–40}
{key: D}
{tempo: 114}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [D] | [A] | [Bm] |
| [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Down from the Mount of Olives [A]on a borrowed colt he rides
[Bm]No sword and no chariot, [G]no soldiers at his side
[D]The people throw their cloaks out [A]on the dusty road ahead
[Bm]They cut the branches from the [G]trees and lay them down instead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Say to the daughter [A]of Zion
[Dmaj7/F#]Look, your king is [G]coming to you
Gentle and rid[A]ing on a [D]donkey
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hosanna to the [A]Son of David
[Bm]Blessed is he who [G]comes in the name of the [D]Lord
Hosanna in the [A]highest
[Bm]Hosanna in the [G]highest
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [D]city wakes and wonders and the [A]question fills the air
[Bm]Who is this that's riding in, [G]who is this coming here
[D]This is Jesus, the [A]prophet from Nazareth in [Bm]Galilee
And [G]save us now, we pray, is the cry from every [A]street
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Dmaj7/F#]Say to the daughter [G]of Zion
Look, your king is coming to [A]you
Gentle and [D]riding on a donkey
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ho[A]sanna to the [Bm]Son of David
Blessed is [G]he who comes in the name of the [D]Lord
Hosanna in the [A]highest
[Bm]Hosanna in the [G]highest
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Teacher, rebuke your [A]disciples
I tell you, [Bm]if they keep silent, [G]the stones will cry out
Peace in heav[A]en and glo[Bm]ry in the high[G]est
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D]Hosanna to the [A]Son of David
[Bm]Hosanna in the [G]highest
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
